./docs/reviews/full-glm.json.raw:3:{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "GLM-5.2", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — Data sent from the client to the MUD via the WebSocket string path has newline appended and is then double-processed by `expandInput` in `TerminalHost.tsx` (called first in `sendLine`, then again inside `useEffect` on inject). If a multi-line alias is used, the injected command is expanded, and each split line is passed to `sendLine` where it is incorrectly expanded again. Furthermore, since `sendLine` sends strings and `escapeIac` correctly handles binary, the double expansion on text commands causes double-execution of multi-line aliases.\napps/proxy/src/policy.ts — In `checkAuth`, if an attacker provides a malformed `authorization` header (e.g., \"bearer \"), it executes `authorization.toLowerCase().startsWith(\"bearer \")`. It then slices it and executes `safeEqual(t, token)`. If `t` is an empty string, it safely mismatches. However, the cookie regex (`/(?:^|;\\s*)assmud_session=([^;]+)/`) may capture malicious payloads if `assmud_session` is spoofed but will safely fail `safeEqual`.\npackages/terminal/src/buffer.ts — `sessionLog` is appended in `lineFeed()` which is only triggered by text containing newline or wrapping; if the buffer session ends without a trailing newline, the final line is omitted from `sessionLog`.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-ze9880", "error": null }
