./docs/reviews/2026-07-21-queue-impl-hetero-all-clear.md:39:1. **probeCjkGlyph**: never accept `document.fonts.check===true` alone; require canvas width ≠ `__AssmudMissingFont__` control.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:7:- Terminal is a **fixed cell grid** (cols×rows via NAWS). Canvas must not CSS-stretch and freckle glyphs.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:8:- Footer always has: command `<input>` + Send + thumb chips (n/s/e/w/look/score) + map toggle on sm.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:10:- Soft keyboard on iOS/Android can cover 40–50% of the viewport; `100vh` / `height:100%` often wrong when keyboard open.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:14:1. Portrait + keyboard: terminal stage does not reliably shrink; content/chrome may overflow the visual viewport.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:21:**A. Portrait default layout** — wireframe regions top→bottom with approximate % of *visual* viewport (not layout viewport). What collapses when keyboard opens?
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:23:**B. Keyboard strategy** — `visualViewport` resize? `dvh`? hide thumb pad while focused? scroll-into-view on input focus? `interactive-widget=resizes-content`?
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:25:**C. Landscape / "rotate" button** — when to show; use Screen Orientation API lock vs CSS-only dual layout; fallback if lock denied; should landscape hide header/thumb and maximize terminal cols?
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:29:**E. Movement** — keep n/s/e/w chips vs 3×3 D-pad vs swipe on canvas; portrait vs landscape difference.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:31:**F. Must-fix top 5** for mudgate next PR (file-level if you know: App.tsx footer, tokens.css, index.html viewport, TerminalHost fit).
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-portrait-landscape-prompt.md:33:**G. Anti-patterns** to avoid for MUD specifically (e.g. scaling canvas with CSS, shrinking below readable cols, fighting system keyboard).
./docs/reviews/round1-qwen.md:24:- **NAWS ↔ renderer coupling unspecified.** City map is 25×9, area 31×9. If the browser canvas is 80×24 but the phone is 40×20, NAWS tells the server different sizes. The plan doesn't state whether the renderer forces a minimum col/row or lets the server clip. A one-line rule in architecture.md would prevent surprises.
./docs/reviews/round1-qwen.md:40:- Add NAWS ↔ minimum viewport rule to architecture.md (what happens when phone cols < map width).
