codex
PORTRAIT_LAYOUT: Size the app against the visual viewport. Keyboard closed, for an 800px-tall phone: header 44–48px (6%); terminal stage 610–625px including 6–8px padding (76–78%); command row 52px; thumb row 48px; safe-area/padding 12–24px (footer total ≈16–18%). Keyboard open, for ≈430px visible height: compact header 36px (8%); terminal gets all remaining flexible space, ideally 320–335px (74–78%); command row 52–56px (13%); thumb row, map toggle, copy toolbar, and decorative stage padding collapse. Never reserve a fixed terminal percentage: use `grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0,1fr) auto`, and let the terminal consume the remainder.

KEYBOARD: Add `interactive-widget=resizes-content` to the viewport meta as progressive enhancement, but do not depend on it alone. Drive `--app-vh` from `window.visualViewport.height` and account for `visualViewport.offsetTop`; listen to both `resize` and `scroll`, batch updates with `requestAnimationFrame`, and set the root shell to `height: var(--app-vh, 100dvh); overflow:hidden`. Use `100dvh` as fallback, not `100vh` or inherited `height:100%`. Detect keyboard-open approximately when `innerHeight - visualViewport.height > 120px` while the command input is focused. In that state hide the thumb row and terminal toolbar, compact the header, remove stage padding, and immediately refit the grid/NAWS. Call `input.scrollIntoView({block:"nearest"})` only after focus if its bounding rect is outside the visual viewport; do not force-scroll the page on every focus. `visualViewport` exposes the viewport actually visible after zoom/keyboard changes, while the Virtual Keyboard API remains limited availability, so it should not be the primary path. [Visual Viewport](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VisualViewport), [Virtual Keyboard API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VirtualKeyboard_API)

LANDSCAPE: Show a rotate/play button on coarse-pointer phones when portrait and the terminal fits fewer than about 64 columns, plus keep it available in settings. Its primary action should explain “橫向遊玩” and attempt fullscreen followed by `screen.orientation.lock("landscape")` from the user gesture. Treat rejection as normal: show a brief “請旋轉裝置” overlay and let CSS `@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 520px)` provide the real layout. Orientation lock has limited availability and commonly requires fullscreen, so CSS must remain authoritative. In landscape use a 32–36px compact header or auto-hide it after 2 seconds; keep status/gear as overlay controls; hide tab labels, copy buttons, `look`/`score`, and map panel by default. Use a 44–48px command row and place four movement controls as a right-side rail or compact overlay. Give the terminal the remaining width and height, targeting roughly 70–100 cols without CSS scaling. Do not permanently force landscape or hide all navigation with no way back. [Screen orientation lock](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ScreenOrientation/lock), [CSS orientation layouts](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSS_Object_Model/Managing_screen_orientation)

CMD_BAR: Keep a single-line `<input>`; MUD commands are short and multiline expansion would steal live-output rows. Do not expand it on focus. Use 16px input text on iOS to avoid focus zoom, 44–48px minimum row height, and a 48–56px-wide Send button—current `min-width:4.5rem` is unnecessarily expensive on narrow screens. Preserve `enterKeyHint="send"`, IME composition handling, password masking, and history draft restoration. Support history with explicit ↑/↓ affordance or a vertical swipe that begins on the input only: swipe down = older, up = newer, with a 28–36px threshold and no action during horizontal cursor movement or IME composition. Never bind canvas swipes to command history.

MOVEMENT: Keep the six chips for portrait keyboard-closed, but make them one non-wrapping 44px-high horizontal row; wrapping is the current vertical-space failure. Put `n/s/e/w` first and allow `look/score/map` to scroll horizontally. Hide that row while the soft keyboard is open. Do not use a 3×3 D-pad below the command bar in portrait—it costs roughly 136–152px. Do not make canvas swipe the only movement method because it conflicts with scrollback, selection, map interaction, and accidental combat movement. In landscape, use a compact 3×3 D-pad or four-way side rail outside the canvas; optional canvas swipe may be opt-in, require a clear 40–50px gesture, and provide visual confirmation.

MUST_FIX:
1. In `apps/web/src/App.tsx`, introduce visual-viewport/keyboard state and make the play shell a bounded `minmax(0,1fr)` layout. Compact the header and conditionally collapse thumb/terminal chrome while the command input is focused and the keyboard is detected.
2. In `apps/web/src/styles/tokens.css` and `index.css`, replace the `html, body, #root { height:100% }` dependency with `--app-vh`, `100dvh` fallback, `overflow:hidden`, mobile `--topbar-h/--cmd-h` tokens, safe-area handling, and portrait/short-landscape media queries.
3. In `apps/web/index.html`, append `interactive-widget=resizes-content` to the existing `viewport-fit=cover` viewport declaration. Keep VisualViewport handling because browser behavior still differs.
4. In `apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx` and `lib/termFit.ts`, refit on every actual wrapper resize and visual-viewport transition, debounce NAWS until geometry settles, and remove the dangerous effective overflow caused by clamping to `minRows:12` when fewer than 12 rows physically fit. The reported grid must never be larger than the canvas area; permit a temporary 4–6-row emergency grid with the keyboard open.
5. In `App.tsx` footer and `TerminalHost.tsx` toolbar, make chips non-wrapping, reduce Send width, hide the thumb row during keyboard entry, replace the three always-visible copy buttons with one 44px overflow/copy action on small screens, and add the portrait-only landscape-play control with CSS fallback.

ANTI:
- Never CSS-scale the canvas to fit a desired 80×24 grid; resize the backing grid and send the real cols×rows through NAWS.
- Never clamp cols/rows upward beyond what the measured stage can contain; `overflow:hidden` merely conceals the resulting clipped grid.
- Never reduce the terminal font until 80 columns fit portrait. Prefer approximately 40–48 readable columns in portrait and use landscape for the classic ~80-column experience.
- Never use `100vh`, fixed footer offsets, or body scrolling as the keyboard layout model.
- Never chase the keyboard with repeated `scrollIntoView()` calls or attempt to dismiss/control the system keyboard.
- Never stack header, toolbar, multiline command field, wrapped chips, and map controls above/below the terminal simultaneously.
- Never make swipe-to-move the default over selectable/scrollable terminal output.
- Never send continuous NAWS updates for every noisy viewport pixel; coalesce and send only changed stable cell geometry.

ONE_LINE: Portrait should be a readable 40–48-col terminal with disposable chrome; landscape should be the deliberate ~80-col play mode, and both must derive their grid from the live visual viewport rather than stretching canvas pixels.

